      "content": "That relief you feel is a clue that you are already on the right track to finding \"peace\" not as a happy ending, but as a **resignation with hopelessness that no longer hurts him to accept.**\n\nTo describe this, avoid making it a quiet \"good ending\" and instead focus on the **heavy silence of release**, where the burden of \"what if\" is finally gone, leaving only the \"that is.\"\n\nYou can make that moment feel defintive and real by letting his final action be the **acceptance of the end itself** without any attempt to fight it or feel sorry for it.",
